// REFINED-SORT elim at a CONSTANT witness — the guard is discharged EXPLICITLY.
//
// `forall_elim(c)` over a refined universal `forall h: H` yields `good(c) -> f(c) = c`.
// bpa is an EXPLICIT prover: the author establishes `good(c)` as a step (here from the
// axiom `goodC`), and the refined-sort auto-discharge then folds it — the elim's guard
// matches the prior `good(c)` step, so the conclusion step claims the bare `f(c) = c`.
// (No global fact SEARCH — the guard is an ordinary obligation, cited like any other.)
sort G
pred good(x: G)
sort H = G where good
const c: G
func f(x: G): G

axiom goodC: good(c)
axiom fLaw: forall h: H; f(h) = h

theorem fAtConst: f(c) = c
proof
  @c-is-good |
    good(c)
    [by cite goodC]
  @the-law |
    forall h: H; f(h) = h
    [by cite fLaw]
  @conclusion |
    f(c) = c
    [by forall_elim(c) the-law]
qed
